---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/10-09/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/10-09/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/10-09/',base='https://www.intantech.com/image-src/',spec='https://www.intantech.com/stim_record_controller.html',heads='https://intantech.com/RHS_headstages.html';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="Intan RHS read-only playback bench" subtitle="" description="Inspect a metric Intan M4200 rack and compare fixed synthetic timelines with no hardware access." wide={true}>
<article id="rhs" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-09/">← Equipment 10-09</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#rhs-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">10-09 / Intan M4200 + RHS headstage silhouettes / Read-only traces</p><h2>Intan RHS playback</h2><p>Open a fixed synthetic bench trace and compare timestamp markers by channel. A-01 marks 20 ms and B-01 marks 23 ms, a +3 ms offset. No connected instrument or electrical output is involved.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the rack and ports</h3><div id="rhs-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Rear','Headstage'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="rhs-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="rhs-model" aria-label="Orbitable Intan rack silhouette with clickable port and red headstage targets for read-only replay"></canvas><p id="rhs-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click a port or red carrier card to select its stored channel. Port D is empty. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. Other rear and front hardware details are decorative.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Choose a stored channel</h3><form id="rhs-form"><div class="e-fields"><label>Channel<select id="rhs-channel">{['A-01','A-02','B-01','C-01','A-32','D-01'].map(k=><option value={k}>{k}</option>)}</select></label></div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="rhs-read" class="e-run" type="submit">Read synthetic trace</button><button id="rhs-align" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Align labels to A-01 marker</button><button id="rhs-reset" type="button">Reset selection</button></div></form><p id="rhs-status" role="status">No trace loaded.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read the native timestamps</h3><p id="rhs-result" role="status">No samples available.</p><svg id="rhs-chart" viewBox="0 0 432 202" role="img" aria-label="Selected synthetic playback voltage, dashed primary reference, and selected fiducial"></svg><div class="e-row"><button id="rhs-json" disabled>Waveform JSON</button><button id="rhs-csv" disabled>Waveform CSV</button></div>
<p>Teal is the selected trace, gray dashes are the A-01 reference, and the rust line is the selected fiducial. Alignment moves the axis labels to the A-01 marker; original sample timestamps and amplitudes are unchanged. <a href={a+'example-trace.json'}>Example JSON</a> · Import waveform JSON at the <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/">Tektronix 09-04 station</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Reference configuration</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original front M4200 and three compact red cable witnesses"/><figcaption>Original front geometry based on the manufacturer’s <a href={base+'front_panel_RHS_4SPI_904.jpg'}>four-port panel</a>. Modeled witness cables are shortened for the layout.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Intan rack rear geometry"/><figcaption>Original cosmetic rear based on the manufacturer’s <a href={base+'back_panel_USB2_904.jpg'}>rear panel photograph</a>. No connectors transact data here.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Reference</th><th>Modeled</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Intan M4200 chassis</td><td><a href={spec}>Intan product reference</a>: standard 19-inch rack, 1U</td><td>Nominal rack face width 482.6 mm; 43.4 mm enclosure height and ~190 mm depth are estimates. Four front port targets.</td></tr><tr><td>M4032 on A and C</td><td><a href={heads}>Intan headstage specification</a>: 24 × 15 mm</td><td>Two original red 32-channel-class dummy board outlines.</td></tr><tr><td>M4016 on B</td><td>Same source: 24 × 13 mm</td><td>One original 16-channel-class dummy board outline. D empty.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>Playback scope</h3><p>The synthetic fixture stores 121 zero-based samples at 0.5 ms spacing for four labels only. Detection uses the first magnitude crossing at 5 mV in fixed data, not a trigger setting or electrical delivery parameter. A-32 is a valid channel label but has no trace in this file; D-01 is unavailable because that port is empty. Neither case generates values. The virtual trace labels are not measurements of the actual Intan system.</p><p>No stimulation, recording from hardware, current events, impedance, noise model, implant, biological protocol or rack access is simulated. The catalogue’s biphasic electrical acceptance is outside this read-only pass.</p></section>
<section id="rhs-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'intan-rhs-m4200.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-09/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#rhs header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#rhs h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#rhs section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#rhs button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#rhs button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#rhs-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#rhs-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#rhs table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#rhs td,#rhs th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#rhs figure{margin:0}#rhs img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#rhs caption{text-align:left}#rhs input,#rhs select,#rhs button{min-width:0}#rhs .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}</style>
